Question : 766. Toeplitz Matrix
Given an m x n matrix, return true if the matrix is Toeplitz. Otherwise, return false.
A matrix is Toeplitz if every diagonal from top-left to bottom-right has the same elements.

Explanation : 
This was a simple question where I solved it with two nested for loops and checked the next [i+1][j+1]th element for whether it was equal : if equal we continued 
else returned false.

Time complexity : O(m*n)
Space complexity : O(1)

Solution :
class Solution {
public:
    bool isToeplitzMatrix(vector<vector<int>>& matrix) {
        int m=matrix.size(),n=matrix[0].size();
        for(int i=0;i<m;i++){
            for(int j=0;j<n;j++){
                if(i<m-1 and j<n-1){
                    if(matrix[i+1][j+1]==matrix[i][j]){
                        continue;
                    }
                    else{
                        return false;
                    }
                }
            }
        }
        return true;
    }
};

Question : 566. Reshape the Matrix
In MATLAB, there is a handy function called reshape which can reshape an m x n matrix into a new one with a different size r x c keeping its original data.
You are given an m x n matrix mat and two integers r and c representing the number of rows and the number of columns of the wanted reshaped matrix.
The reshaped matrix should be filled with all the elements of the original matrix in the same row-traversing order as they were.
If the reshape operation with given parameters is possible and legal, output the new reshaped matrix; Otherwise, output the original matrix.

Explanation : 
This was also a simple question where we had to insert elements into a given sized array while preserving the row-traversing order that is if we would have to 
write elements in a single line while accessing them one row after another, this single line of elements should be same for both the arrays (given and created)
if thats not the same then we return the same matrix.
I used two nested for loops and an if-else condition to increment the new matrix's traversal(as shown in code).

Time complexity : O(m*n)
Space complexity : O(1)

Solution : 
class Solution {
public:
    vector<vector<int>> matrixReshape(vector<vector<int>>& mat, int r, int c) {
        int m=mat.size(),n=mat[0].size(),p=0,q=0;
        vector<vector<int>>ans(r,vector<int>(c));
        if(m*n==(r*c)){
            for(int i=0;i<m;i++){
                for(int j=0;j<n;j++){
                    ans[p][q]=mat[i][j];
                    if(q==c-1){
                        q=0;
                        p++;
                    }
                    else{
                        q++;
                    }
                }
            }
            return ans;
        }
        return mat;
    }
};
